          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              , chapter 6 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supgergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
          %h3#ReferencesInSYM In (super-)Yang-Mills theory
          %p It was originally noticed in
          %ul
            %li#GNO77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Goddard"}> Peter Goddard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Nuyts"} Jean Nuyts
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Olive"} David Olive
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge Theories And Magnetic Charge
              %strong 125
              (1977) 1-28 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(77)90221-8"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(77)90221-8
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/111435"} spire:111435
          %p
            that where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+charge"} electric charge
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            takes values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+lattice"} weight lattice
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            takes values in the lattice of what is now called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+dual+group"} Langlands dual group
          %p This led to the electric/magnetic duality conjecture formulation in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claus+Montonen"}> Claus Montonen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Olive"} David Olive
              %em Magnetic Monopoles As Gauge Particles?
              Phys. Lett. B72 (1977) 117-120.
          %p
            According to (
            %a{:href => "#KapustinWitten06"}> Kapustin-Witten 06, pages 3-4
            ) the observaton that the Montonen-Olive dual charge group coincides with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+dual+group"} Langlands dual group
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              , private communication to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
          %p
            Discussion of the duality for abelian gauge theory (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"}> electromagnetism
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em On S-duality in abelian gauge theory
                Selecta Mathematica, (2):383-410, 1995 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9505186"}> arXiv:hep-th/9505186
                )
            %li
              %p
                Jose Barbon,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized abelian S-duality and coset constructions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506137"} arXiv:hep-th/9506137
            %li
              %p
                Gerald Kelnhofer,
                %em Functional integration and gauge ambiguities in generalized abelian gauge theories
                J. Geom. Physics, 59:1017-1035, 200
          %p
            and for its non-linear
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI+theory"} DBI theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
                , D. A. Rasheed:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Electric-Magnetic Duality Rotations in Non-Linear Electrodynamics
                %strong 454
                1-2 (1995) 185-206 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506035"}> arXiv:hep-th/9506035
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(95)00409-L"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(95)00409-L
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
                , D. A. Rasheed:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{R})
                    Invariance of Non-Linear Electrodynamics Coupled to An Axion and a Dilaton
                %strong 365
                1-4 (1996) 46-50 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9509141"}> arXiv:hep-th/9509141
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(95)01272-9"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(95)01272-9
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electro-magnetic+duality"} electro-magnetic duality
          %p
            The insight that the Montonen-Olive duality works more naturally in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Olive"}> David Olive
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetry Algebras That Include Topological Charges
          %p
            and that it works particularly for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=4 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              H. Osborn,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Topological Charges For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 4
                  Supersymmetric Gauge Theories And Monopoles Of Spin 1
          %p with further computations in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Strong Coupling Test of S-Duality
              %strong 431
              (1994) 3-77 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408074"}> arXiv:hep-th/9408074
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The observation that the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            electric/magnetic duality extends to an
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Cardy"}> John Cardy
                , E. Rabinovici,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Phase Structure Of Zp Models In The Presence Of A Theta Parameter
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Cardy"}> John Cardy
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality And The Theta Parameter In Abelian Lattice Models
            %li
              %p
                A. Shapere and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Wilczek"} Frank Wilczek
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Selfdual Models With Theta Terms
          %p
            The understanding of this
            = succeed "-symmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            – compactified on a torus is described in
          %ul
            %li#Witten95a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , pages 4-5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some Comments On String Dynamics
                %em String95
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hepth/9507121"}> arXiv:hepth/9507121
                )
            %li#Witten95b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em On S-Duality in Abelian Gauge Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9505186"}> arXiv:hep-th/9505186
                )
            %li#Witten07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conformal+field+theory+in+four+and+six+dimensions"} Conformal field theory in four and six dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.0157"}> arXiv:0712.0157
                )
          %p
            On an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algorithm"} algorithm
            for constructing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-dual
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+gauge+theories"} quiver gauge theories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Chiung Hwang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sara+Pasquetti"} Sara Pasquetti
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rethinking mirror symmetry as a local duality on fields
                %strong 106
                (2022) 105014 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.11362"}> arXiv:2110.11362
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.106.105014"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.106.105014
            %li
              %p
                Riccardo Comi, Chiung Hwang, Fabio Marino,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sara+Pasquetti"} Sara Pasquetti
                %em
                  The
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2, \mathbb{Z})
                  dualization algorithm at work
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.10571"}> arXiv:2212.10571
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#in_type_ii_superstring_theory In type II superstring theory
          %p
            The suggestion of an
            = succeed "-duality" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring+theory"} type II superstring theory
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"} Ashoke Sen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Duality Symmetries Of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4D
                    Heterotic Strings
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                %em
                  Dyon - Monopole Bound States, Self-Dual Harmonic Forms on the Multi-Monopole Moduli Space, and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
                  Invariance in String Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9402032"}> arXiv:hep-th/9402032
                )
          %p
            %em> Duality Symmetric Actions
            , Nucl. Phys. B411 (1994) 35-63 (
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304154"}> arXiv:hep-th/9304154
            )
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Unity of Superstring Dualities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9410167"} arXiv:hep-th/9410167
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    An
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
                    Multiplet of Type IIB Superstrings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9508143"} arXiv:hep-th/9508143
          %p
            The geometric understanding of S-duality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring+theory"} type II superstring theory
            via
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            goes maybe back to
          %ul
            %li#Johnson97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From M-theory to F-theory, with Branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706155"} arXiv:hep-th/9706155
          %p A textbook account is in
          %ul
            %li#West12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+West"}> Peter West
              , section 17.3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Strings+and+Branes"} Introduction to Strings and Branes
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-loop"} 2-loop
            test is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
              , Michael Gutperle,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
              = succeed "," do
                %em Two-loop superstrings and S-duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0503180"} arXiv:hep-th/0503180
          %p
            S-duality acting on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            theory if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28p%2Cq%29-strings"} (p,q)-strings
            is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Bandos00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superembedding Approach and S-Duality. A unified description of superstring and super-D1-brane
              %strong 599
              197-227 (2001) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0008249"}> arXiv:hep-th/0008249
              )
          %p
            Closely related to this, S-duality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            as an operation on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+spacetime"} extended super spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super L-infinity algebra
            is
          %ul
            %li#FSS13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"}> arXiv:1308.5264
              )
          %p The cohomological problem of the type II S-duality action on the 3-form flux was originally highlighted in
          %ul
            %li#DMW00
              D. Diaconescu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                  Gauge Theory, and a Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005090"} arXiv:hep-th/0005090
          %p
            The conjecture that with combined targetspace/worldsheet modular transformations the type IIB S-duality is reflected in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#KrizSati05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"}> Igor Kriz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %em Type II string theory and modularity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501060"} arXiv:hep-th/0501060
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#BEJVS05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bouwknegt"}> Peter Bouwknegt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarah+Evslin"} Jarah Evslin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"} Branislav Jurco
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathai+Varghese"} Mathai Varghese
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flux Compactifications on Projective Spaces and The S-Duality Puzzle
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501110"} arXiv:hep-th/0501110
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Montonen-Olive+duality"} Montonen-Olive duality
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM-model"} ABJM-model
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3-brane"} D3-brane
            model after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            followed by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koji+Hashimoto"}> Koji Hashimoto
              , Ta-Sheng Tai,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiji+Terashima"} Seiji Terashima
              = succeed "," do
                %em Toward a Proof of Montonen-Olive Duality via Multiple M2-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0809.2137"} arxiv:0809.2137
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Surya Raghavendran, Philsang Yoo,
              %em Twisted S-Duality
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.13653"}> arxiv:1910.13653
              )
          %h3#in_heterotic_string_theory In heterotic string theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+corrections"} higher curvature corrections
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohammad+R.+Garousi"}> Mohammad R. Garousi
              \:
              %em S-duality in higher-derivative corrections of heterotic supergravity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00357"}> arXiv:2502.00357
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#relation_to_geometric_langlands_duality Relation to geometric Langlands duality
          %p
            The relation of S-duality to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+duality"} geometric Langlands duality
            was understood in
          %ul
            %li#KapustinWitten06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              %em Electric-Magnetic Duality And The Geometric Langlands Program
              , Communications in number theory and physics, Volume 1, Number 1, 1–236 (2007) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0604151"}> arXiv:hep-th/0604151
              )
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
              ,
              %em What Do Fermat’s Last Theorem and Electro-magnetic Duality Have in Common?
              KITP talk 2011 (
              %a{:href => "http://online.kitp.ucsb.edu/online/bblunch/frenkel/"}> web
              )
        .revisedby
